.TH TAXIPRIJS 1 "2026" "taxiprijs 2.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
taxiprijs \- Dutch taxi fare calculator TUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B taxiprijs
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B taxiprijs
is a terminal user interface application for calculating taxi fares in the Netherlands.
.PP
It supports configurable pricing for different passenger groups and uses TOML for configuration.
.PP
The home screen is the fare form. Press 1 or click
.B ▸ Menu
to open the menu (Settings, Help, updates, branch switch, uninstall, report issue).
Press 2 or click
.B ⌫ Clear
to empty the fare fields. Addresses stay filled after a calculation until cleared.
.SH OPTIONS
.B taxiprijs
does not take any command line options.
.SH INSTALLATION
TaxiCheck can be installed as a snap or flatpak, or from source.
.TP
.B Snap
.B sudo snap install taxiprijs
.br
Run it with
.B taxiprijs
or from the application menu. The snap is strictly confined with
.B network
and
.B home
plugs so it can reach the routing/geocoding APIs and read/write
.B ~/.taxiprijs
.
To install a locally built snap:
.B sudo snap install --dangerous taxiprijs_2.0.1_amd64.snap
.TP
.B Flatpak
.B flatpak install flathub dev.ramackers.TaxiCheck
.br
Run it with
.B flatpak run dev.ramackers.TaxiCheck
. The flatpak is granted
.B --share=network
and
.B --filesystem=~/.taxiprijs:create
. To install a locally built bundle:
.B flatpak install --user taxiprijs-flatpak-2.0.1.flatpak
.TP
.B From source
.B git clone https://github.com/ramackersjp/taxiCheck.git && cd taxiCheck && git checkout v2.0.1
.br
Then
.B make install
or build with
.B go build -o taxiprijs ./cmd/taxiprijs
and run
.B ./taxiprijs
.
.SH KEYBOARD CONTROLS
.TP
.B 1
Open the menu from home (press Esc first if a fare field is focused)
.TP
.B 2
Clear fare fields on home (press Esc first if a fare field is focused)
.TP
.B 1
Settings (on the menu page)
.TP
.B 2
Help/Manual (on the menu page)
.TP
.B 3
Check for updates (GitHub) (on the menu page)
.TP
.B 4
Switch branch (dev / stable) (on the menu page)
.TP
.B 5
Uninstall (on the menu page)
.TP
.B 6
Report issue (on the menu page)
.TP
.B q
Quit (from the menu page, or from home when fields are not focused)
.TP
.B Tab
Next input field
.TP
.B Shift+Tab
Previous input field
.TP
.B Enter
Submit/Save
.TP
.B Esc
Back/Cancel
.SH UPDATE & BRANCHES
The application can check for updates on GitHub and pull them directly.
After a successful pull the binary is rebuilt and installed automatically,
so the next launch runs the new version.
.PP
Branches available:
.TP
.B dev
Development branch - may be unstable
.TP
.B v2.0.1
Stable release branch
.PP
Stable release branches (e.g. v2.0.1) are listed and can be
switched to from the TUI; local changes are stashed before the switch and
restored afterwards.
.SH REPORTING ISSUES
Option 6 in the main menu starts a report.
.PP
Enter a problem description and, if available, the error output. The report is
always saved to
.B ~/.taxiprijs/logs/
and, when the
.B gh
CLI is installed and the repository has a GitHub remote, filed as a GitHub
issue whose number is shown after submission.
.SH UNINSTALLING
Option 5 in the main menu starts the uninstall process.
.PP
The uninstall requires two confirmations for safety:
.IP 1. 3
First: "Are you sure you want to uninstall?" (y/n)
.IP 2. 3
Second: "WARNING: This will remove all files. Are you REALLY sure?" (y/n)
.PP
After both confirmations, the binary and desktop entry are removed via
.BR make uninstall (1).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is stored in
.B ~/.taxiprijs/config.toml
.PP
The TOML file can be edited manually or through the Settings screen.
.PP
Example configuration:
.PP
.RS
[[passenger_groups]]
.br
name = "1-4 passengers"
.br
board_fee = 3.50
.br
per_minute = 0.50
.br
wait_minute = 0.50
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.taxiprijs/config.toml
User configuration file
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Calculate a fare:
.IP 1. 3
Start the application
.IP 2. 3
The fare form is already on the home screen; optionally press 1 for the menu
.IP 3. 3
Enter start address (e.g. "Dam Square, Amsterdam")
.IP 4. 3
Enter destination (e.g. "Central Station, Rotterdam")
.IP 5. 3
Enter number of passengers (1-8)
.IP 6. 3
Press Enter to calculate
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit
.TP
.B 1
Error occurred
